1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,069
It's six thirty in the morning.

2
00:00:01,969 --> 00:00:03,758
Your alarm goes off... once.

3
00:00:03,838 --> 00:00:05,206
And you actually get up.

4
00:00:05,286 --> 00:00:06,862
No snooze. No panic.

5
00:00:06,762 --> 00:00:08,927
No racing heart. Just... up.

6
00:00:09,007 --> 00:00:11,005
You even have time to make the bed.

7
00:00:11,185 --> 00:00:13,774
Across town, Jake's alarm goes off at

8
00:00:13,674 --> 00:00:15,119
the exact same time.

9
00:00:15,199 --> 00:00:17,423
He hits snooze. Then again. And again.

10
00:00:17,503 --> 00:00:19,766
Every nine minutes, the same little fight

11
00:00:19,666 --> 00:00:20,557
with his phone.

12
00:00:20,637 --> 00:00:22,859
And every time, he tells himself...

13
00:00:22,759 --> 00:00:24,254
just five more minutes.

14
00:00:24,434 --> 00:00:26,341
By the time he opens his eyes

15
00:00:26,241 --> 00:00:28,024
for real, it's eight fifty.

16
00:00:28,104 --> 00:00:29,747
His meeting starts at nine.

17
00:00:29,827 --> 00:00:32,459
He's late. Again. Third time this month.

18
00:00:32,639 --> 00:00:34,780
And here's the thing nobody tells you.

19
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:37,235
Jake's messy morning isn't just stressful.

20
00:00:37,315 --> 00:00:38,861
It's costing him money.

21
00:00:38,761 --> 00:00:40,685
Real money. Every single day.

22
00:00:40,765 --> 00:00:43,187
Not in one big painful moment.

23
00:00:43,087 --> 00:00:45,199
In tiny, invisible pieces.

24
00:00:45,379 --> 00:00:47,304
Stay with me, because by the end

25
00:00:47,204 --> 00:00:49,699
of this story you'll see exactly how much.

26
00:00:49,779 --> 00:00:52,073
And the simple morning routine that makes

27
00:00:51,973 --> 00:00:53,678
you calmer, more productive...

28
00:00:53,758 --> 00:00:57,215
and about three thousand dollars richer every single year.

29
00:00:57,395 --> 00:00:59,622
So let's rewind. Let's go back to

30
00:00:59,522 --> 00:01:00,718
the night before.

31
00:01:00,798 --> 00:01:03,250
Because a good morning doesn't actually start

32
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:04,034
in the morning.

33
00:01:04,114 --> 00:01:06,817
It starts around nine thirty the evening before.

34
00:01:06,897 --> 00:01:08,826
Sounds boring? Stick with me.

35
00:01:08,726 --> 00:01:10,845
This is where the magic happens.

36
00:01:11,025 --> 00:01:12,948
You give it ten minutes. That's all.

37
00:01:13,028 --> 00:01:15,406
You lay out tomorrow's clothes on the chair.

38
00:01:15,486 --> 00:01:16,711
You pack your lunch.

39
00:01:16,611 --> 00:01:19,188
You fill the coffee maker and set the timer.

40
00:01:19,368 --> 00:01:21,995
Keys, wallet, badge... all in one little

41
00:01:21,895 --> 00:01:23,069
bowl by the door.

42
00:01:23,149 --> 00:01:25,012
It feels almost too simple, right?

43
00:01:25,092 --> 00:01:27,310
But every decision you make tonight is

44
00:01:27,210 --> 00:01:29,483
one you don't have to make half asleep.

45
00:01:29,563 --> 00:01:31,138
No searching. No stress.

46
00:01:31,038 --> 00:01:33,473
Everything is right where you left it.

47
00:01:33,653 --> 00:01:35,436
And then you do one more thing.

48
00:01:35,336 --> 00:01:36,087
The big one.

49
00:01:36,167 --> 00:01:37,664
You plug your phone in...

50
00:01:37,564 --> 00:01:38,559
across the room.

51
00:01:38,639 --> 00:01:39,823
Not on your pillow.

52
00:01:39,723 --> 00:01:40,794
Not in your hand.

53
00:01:40,694 --> 00:01:41,707
Across the room.

54
00:01:41,887 --> 00:01:44,317
Why? Because now, when the alarm rings,

55
00:01:44,217 --> 00:01:46,468
you have to stand up to turn it off.

56
00:01:46,548 --> 00:01:47,878
And once you're standing?

57
00:01:47,958 --> 00:01:50,497
Honestly... the hardest part of the morning

58
00:01:50,397 --> 00:01:51,404
is already over.

59
00:01:51,584 --> 00:01:53,862
Meanwhile, Jake is in bed. Scrolling.

60
00:01:53,942 --> 00:01:56,653
Eleven thirty. Midnight. Twelve forty.

61
00:01:56,733 --> 00:01:58,801
One more video. Just one more.

62
00:01:58,881 --> 00:02:00,655
His brain is wide awake.

63
00:02:00,555 --> 00:02:02,749
His body is begging for sleep.

64
00:02:02,929 --> 00:02:05,026
Most adults need at least seven hours

65
00:02:04,926 --> 00:02:05,943
of sleep a night.

66
00:02:06,023 --> 00:02:07,288
Jake gets about six.

67
00:02:07,188 --> 00:02:08,859
And that's on a good night.

68
00:02:08,939 --> 00:02:10,995
He doesn't feel tired at midnight.

69
00:02:10,895 --> 00:02:12,203
He feels it at seven.

70
00:02:12,283 --> 00:02:14,720
So every morning starts with a little sleep debt.

71
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:16,234
So the next morning,

72
00:02:16,134 --> 00:02:18,824
that snooze button feels like a lifesaver.

73
00:02:18,904 --> 00:02:20,257
Just nine more minutes.

74
00:02:20,157 --> 00:02:21,348
What could go wrong?

75
00:02:21,428 --> 00:02:22,977
But it isn't a lifesaver.

76
00:02:22,877 --> 00:02:23,673
It's a trap.

77
00:02:23,853 --> 00:02:26,754
Those extra minutes don't give you real, deep rest.

78
00:02:26,834 --> 00:02:28,343
You just drift in and out,

79
00:02:28,243 --> 00:02:29,047
in and out...

80
00:02:29,127 --> 00:02:31,595
and you wake up even groggier than before.

81
00:02:31,775 --> 00:02:33,394
And then the scramble begins.

82
00:02:33,474 --> 00:02:35,414
No clean shirt. No breakfast.

83
00:02:35,314 --> 00:02:37,064
Keys? Where are the keys?!

84
00:02:37,144 --> 00:02:39,543
He finds them in yesterday's jeans.

85
00:02:39,443 --> 00:02:40,397
On the floor.

86
00:02:40,477 --> 00:02:42,627
His heart is pounding before he even

87
00:02:42,527 --> 00:02:43,822
leaves the apartment.

88
00:02:44,002 --> 00:02:45,893
He runs out the door with nothing.

89
00:02:45,973 --> 00:02:47,417
No coffee. No food.

90
00:02:47,317 --> 00:02:48,832
No plan for the day.

91
00:02:48,912 --> 00:02:50,995
Just stress. And a growing headache.

92
00:02:51,175 --> 00:02:53,869
And that's exactly where his wallet starts bleeding.

93
00:02:53,949 --> 00:02:56,580
Quietly. Politely. Every single morning.

94
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:57,596
Watch this.

95
00:02:57,676 --> 00:02:58,834
And the worst part?

96
00:02:58,734 --> 00:03:00,838
He doesn't even notice it happening.

97
00:03:01,018 --> 00:03:03,909
Stop number one: the coffee shop on the corner.

98
00:03:03,989 --> 00:03:05,603
There's a line, of course.

99
00:03:05,503 --> 00:03:06,767
He's even later now.

100
00:03:06,847 --> 00:03:09,090
A large latte. Six dollars.

101
00:03:09,270 --> 00:03:11,646
Stop number two: a breakfast sandwich,

102
00:03:11,546 --> 00:03:12,964
because he's starving.

103
00:03:13,044 --> 00:03:15,079
He eats it in four bites, walking.

104
00:03:15,159 --> 00:03:16,130
Eight dollars.

105
00:03:16,310 --> 00:03:19,105
Fourteen dollars. Gone before nine A M.

106
00:03:19,185 --> 00:03:20,780
Does that sound like a lot?

107
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:23,070
Not really, right? It's just breakfast.

108
00:03:23,150 --> 00:03:25,755
And honestly, Jake would say the same thing.

109
00:03:25,935 --> 00:03:27,351
But let's do the math.

110
00:03:27,251 --> 00:03:29,264
Fourteen dollars, every workday.

111
00:03:29,344 --> 00:03:31,320
About twenty one workdays a month.

112
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:34,865
That's roughly two hundred ninety four dollars. Every month.

113
00:03:35,045 --> 00:03:36,187
Over a full year?

114
00:03:36,087 --> 00:03:38,764
About three thousand five hundred dollars.

115
00:03:38,844 --> 00:03:42,515
Gone. On coffee and sandwiches he barely even tasted.

116
00:03:42,595 --> 00:03:45,656
That's a vacation. That's an emergency fund. Gone.

117
00:03:45,736 --> 00:03:47,345
Think about that for a second.

118
00:03:47,525 --> 00:03:48,879
And you know what's worse?

119
00:03:48,959 --> 00:03:50,845
Jake isn't even enjoying it.

120
00:03:50,925 --> 00:03:52,463
He's eating at his desk,

121
00:03:52,363 --> 00:03:54,800
stressed, already behind on everything.

122
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:56,463
By lunch, he's exhausted.

123
00:03:56,363 --> 00:03:58,005
And he's buying lunch too.

124
00:03:58,185 --> 00:03:59,768
Now. Let's look at your morning.

125
00:03:59,848 --> 00:04:01,506
Same city. Same job.

126
00:04:01,406 --> 00:04:03,221
Same paycheck as Jake.

127
00:04:03,301 --> 00:04:05,450
The only difference is what happens in

128
00:04:05,350 --> 00:04:06,799
the first thirty minutes.

129
00:04:06,979 --> 00:04:08,563
You get up at six thirty.

130
00:04:08,463 --> 00:04:10,047
You walk across the room.

131
00:04:10,127 --> 00:04:11,694
You switch off the alarm.

132
00:04:11,774 --> 00:04:13,704
And then you do something that feels

133
00:04:13,604 --> 00:04:15,942
weird at first... you leave the phone there.

134
00:04:16,022 --> 00:04:18,344
No notifications. No headlines.

135
00:04:18,244 --> 00:04:20,209
Just you and a quiet room.

136
00:04:20,389 --> 00:04:22,722
Because the second you open your phone,

137
00:04:22,622 --> 00:04:24,611
your morning isn't yours anymore.

138
00:04:24,691 --> 00:04:26,533
Emails. News. Group chats.

139
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:28,141
Other people's problems.

140
00:04:28,221 --> 00:04:30,058
You haven't even brushed your teeth,

141
00:04:29,958 --> 00:04:31,410
and you're already stressed.

142
00:04:31,590 --> 00:04:34,356
So instead, you drink a big glass of water.

143
00:04:34,436 --> 00:04:35,778
You open the window.

144
00:04:35,678 --> 00:04:37,020
Cold air. Fresh air.

145
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:39,397
Five slow, deep breaths. That's it.

146
00:04:39,477 --> 00:04:40,880
Your body wakes up.

147
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,320
Your mind slows down.

148
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:44,381
Then you move. Just ten minutes.

149
00:04:44,461 --> 00:04:46,029
A walk around the block.

150
00:04:45,929 --> 00:04:48,538
A few stretches on the living room floor.

151
00:04:48,618 --> 00:04:50,393
Nothing fancy. No gym.

152
00:04:50,293 --> 00:04:51,459
No fancy gear.

153
00:04:51,639 --> 00:04:53,787
You're not training for a marathon here.

154
00:04:53,867 --> 00:04:55,797
You're just telling your body...

155
00:04:55,697 --> 00:04:57,055
hey. It's daytime now.

156
00:04:57,135 --> 00:04:58,783
And by the time you get back,

157
00:04:58,683 --> 00:04:59,957
your head feels clear.

158
00:05:00,037 --> 00:05:02,593
Some mornings you even see the sunrise.

159
00:05:02,493 --> 00:05:04,545
Jake hasn't seen one in months.

160
00:05:04,725 --> 00:05:07,403
Back home, the coffee's already ready and waiting.

161
00:05:07,483 --> 00:05:09,939
Because you set it up last night. Remember?

162
00:05:10,019 --> 00:05:12,513
That smell. Honestly, it's the best part

163
00:05:12,413 --> 00:05:13,171
of the day.

164
00:05:13,351 --> 00:05:15,494
Coffee at home costs you about fifty

165
00:05:15,394 --> 00:05:16,175
cents a cup.

166
00:05:16,255 --> 00:05:17,813
Oatmeal with a banana?

167
00:05:17,713 --> 00:05:19,535
Maybe another fifty cents.

168
00:05:19,615 --> 00:05:21,914
So breakfast costs you about one dollar.

169
00:05:21,994 --> 00:05:23,079
And you know what?

170
00:05:22,979 --> 00:05:25,323
It tastes better than the six dollar one.

171
00:05:25,503 --> 00:05:27,174
One dollar. Sitting down.

172
00:05:27,074 --> 00:05:28,870
Actually tasting your food.

173
00:05:28,950 --> 00:05:32,168
Versus Jake's fourteen dollar sprint down the sidewalk.

174
00:05:32,248 --> 00:05:34,494
Same caffeine. Same full stomach.

175
00:05:34,394 --> 00:05:35,860
Very different price.

176
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:38,620
And now comes the part that changes everything.

177
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:40,075
It takes ten minutes.

178
00:05:39,975 --> 00:05:41,654
And almost nobody does it.

179
00:05:41,734 --> 00:05:43,264
The ten minute money check.

180
00:05:43,444 --> 00:05:45,082
Now you pick up the phone.

181
00:05:44,982 --> 00:05:46,147
But only for this.

182
00:05:46,227 --> 00:05:48,180
Minute one: you look at your balance.

183
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:49,779
No fear. No guessing.

184
00:05:49,679 --> 00:05:51,199
Just the real number.

185
00:05:51,279 --> 00:05:53,146
Ten minutes. One cup of coffee.

186
00:05:53,046 --> 00:05:54,514
That's the whole system.

187
00:05:54,694 --> 00:05:56,474
Next: you check what came out of

188
00:05:56,374 --> 00:05:57,682
your account yesterday.

189
00:05:57,762 --> 00:06:00,723
Anything weird? A charge you don't recognize?

190
00:06:00,803 --> 00:06:03,096
Most days, it's nothing. But today...

191
00:06:03,276 --> 00:06:04,751
Today, you catch something.

192
00:06:04,831 --> 00:06:06,833
A free trial you forgot about.

193
00:06:06,733 --> 00:06:09,624
It just turned into a fifteen dollar charge.

194
00:06:09,704 --> 00:06:12,356
And it would've kept charging you. Every month.

195
00:06:12,436 --> 00:06:14,862
Fifteen dollars a month is one hundred

196
00:06:14,762 --> 00:06:16,209
eighty dollars a year.

197
00:06:16,389 --> 00:06:18,822
You cancel it. Right there. Thirty seconds.

198
00:06:18,902 --> 00:06:20,795
Fifteen dollars a month, saved...

199
00:06:20,875 --> 00:06:22,861
before your coffee is even cold.

200
00:06:22,941 --> 00:06:25,206
If something's tight, you know today.

201
00:06:25,106 --> 00:06:26,025
Not on Friday.

202
00:06:26,205 --> 00:06:27,369
Then you look ahead.

203
00:06:27,449 --> 00:06:29,251
Which bills are due this week?

204
00:06:29,151 --> 00:06:31,010
Rent? Phone? The electric bill?

205
00:06:31,090 --> 00:06:33,037
Is there enough money sitting there for

206
00:06:32,937 --> 00:06:33,606
all of them?

207
00:06:33,686 --> 00:06:35,128
He didn't lack the money.

208
00:06:35,028 --> 00:06:36,201
He just didn't look.

209
00:06:36,381 --> 00:06:37,900
Jake never does this.

210
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:41,036
Last month, he completely forgot his electric bill.

211
00:06:41,116 --> 00:06:42,787
Late fee. Thirty dollars.

212
00:06:42,687 --> 00:06:44,233
For absolutely nothing.

213
00:06:44,413 --> 00:06:46,207
You? You haven't paid a late fee

214
00:06:46,107 --> 00:06:47,000
in over a year.

215
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:49,270
Because you see every bill coming...

216
00:06:49,170 --> 00:06:50,431
days before it hits.

217
00:06:50,511 --> 00:06:53,243
No surprises. No panic. No fees.

218
00:06:53,423 --> 00:06:55,479
And then, the last part of your morning.

219
00:06:55,559 --> 00:06:57,170
You open a little notebook.

220
00:06:57,250 --> 00:06:58,726
And you pick your top three.

221
00:06:58,806 --> 00:07:00,513
Small list. Big days.

222
00:07:00,693 --> 00:07:03,025
Not a to-do list with twenty things

223
00:07:02,925 --> 00:07:04,875
on it. Nobody finishes those.

224
00:07:04,955 --> 00:07:05,971
Just three.

225
00:07:06,051 --> 00:07:08,344
The three things that would make today

226
00:07:08,244 --> 00:07:10,538
a win, even if nothing else gets done.

227
00:07:10,618 --> 00:07:13,460
Because willpower is strongest in the morning.

228
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,832
Use it on what matters.

229
00:07:15,012 --> 00:07:16,299
And the hardest one?

230
00:07:16,199 --> 00:07:17,249
You do it first.

231
00:07:17,329 --> 00:07:19,548
Before the emails. Before the meetings.

232
00:07:19,448 --> 00:07:20,853
Before the noise starts.

233
00:07:20,933 --> 00:07:22,640
While your brain is still fresh.

234
00:07:22,820 --> 00:07:23,654
By ten A M,

235
00:07:23,554 --> 00:07:26,390
your most important work is already done.

236
00:07:26,470 --> 00:07:29,726
And Jake? He's still answering emails from yesterday.

237
00:07:29,806 --> 00:07:32,490
Still on his second coffee. Still behind.

238
00:07:32,570 --> 00:07:34,273
Not because you work longer.

239
00:07:34,173 --> 00:07:35,590
Because you work first.

240
00:07:35,770 --> 00:07:38,224
Your boss notices. Of course she does.

241
00:07:38,304 --> 00:07:39,506
You're the calm one.

242
00:07:39,406 --> 00:07:41,601
The one who actually gets things done.

243
00:07:41,681 --> 00:07:43,084
And people like that...

244
00:07:42,984 --> 00:07:44,671
tend to get the raise first.

245
00:07:44,851 --> 00:07:46,223
So let's do the math.

246
00:07:46,123 --> 00:07:47,434
Just the money part.

247
00:07:47,514 --> 00:07:50,133
Jake spends about three thousand five hundred

248
00:07:50,033 --> 00:07:52,036
dollars a year on rushed mornings.

249
00:07:52,116 --> 00:07:54,210
You spend about two hundred fifty on

250
00:07:54,110 --> 00:07:55,208
breakfast at home.

251
00:07:55,388 --> 00:07:56,355
The difference?

252
00:07:56,435 --> 00:07:59,758
Three thousand two hundred seventy six dollars. Every year.

253
00:07:59,838 --> 00:08:02,652
That's about two hundred seventy three dollars

254
00:08:02,552 --> 00:08:04,894
a month, moved into savings on payday.

255
00:08:04,974 --> 00:08:07,119
Little things. Every single morning.

256
00:08:07,299 --> 00:08:09,614
And that's without counting the late fees

257
00:08:09,514 --> 00:08:10,371
you never pay.

258
00:08:10,451 --> 00:08:12,299
Without the free trials you catch.

259
00:08:12,379 --> 00:08:13,788
And without the stress...

260
00:08:13,688 --> 00:08:15,674
which you can't even put a price on.

261
00:08:15,854 --> 00:08:17,573
Now fast forward one year.

262
00:08:17,653 --> 00:08:19,576
Jake is still running out the door

263
00:08:19,476 --> 00:08:20,380
at eight fifty.

264
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:23,534
Still tired. Still buying the fourteen dollar

265
00:08:23,434 --> 00:08:25,715
breakfast. Still broke by Friday.

266
00:08:25,795 --> 00:08:27,391
Calm mornings. Every day.

267
00:08:27,291 --> 00:08:28,407
For a whole year.

268
00:08:28,587 --> 00:08:30,951
You? You've got over three thousand dollars

269
00:08:30,851 --> 00:08:31,951
sitting in savings.

270
00:08:32,031 --> 00:08:34,019
From mornings. Just... mornings.

271
00:08:34,099 --> 00:08:35,361
You didn't earn more.

272
00:08:35,261 --> 00:08:37,409
You didn't give up anything you love.

273
00:08:37,489 --> 00:08:39,160
Start there. Tomorrow morning,

274
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:40,574
you'll feel the difference.

275
00:08:40,754 --> 00:08:43,142
You just stopped letting your mornings happen to you.

276
00:08:43,222 --> 00:08:45,096
So tonight, try just one thing.

277
00:08:45,176 --> 00:08:46,523
Lay out your clothes.

